WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:16.050
The escape pod shot through space.

2
00:00:19.571 --> 00:00:21.892
Ally kept trying to turn it around, but nothing worked.

3
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:24.773
Then suddenly things got worse.

4
00:00:24.793 --> 00:00:28.135
"Warning: low fuel," the computer said.

5
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:29.735
"How low?"

6
00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:30.676
Ally snapped.

7
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.741
"Must land to refuel."

8
00:00:32.761 --> 00:00:34.923
"Are you kidding me?"

9
00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:37.065
Ally groaned.

10
00:00:38.086 --> 00:00:42.370
"Where's the closest planet to refuel—and get parts to fix the comm device?"

11
00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:44.651
The computer whirred.

12
00:00:44.671 --> 00:00:49.395
"Nearest planet with intelligent life is Earth.

13
00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:52.498
Atmosphere: oxygen.

14
00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.181
Dominant life-form: human, also called Earthling.

15
00:00:56.742 --> 00:01:01.618
Temperament: intelligent, creative, sometimes friendly but often dangerous.

16
00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:05.502
Previous attempts to make contact with humans: unsuccessful.

17
00:01:06.102 --> 00:01:07.343
Deemed too dangerous."

18
00:01:08.324 --> 00:01:08.965
Ally gulped.

19
00:01:10.546 --> 00:01:14.970
"Dangerous?" "Some humans are curious about visitors from other realms.

20
00:01:15.891 --> 00:01:18.834
But most are suspicious and respond with aggression."

21
00:01:18.854 --> 00:01:25.000
"Yikes!" Ally had never heard of a life-form that didn't treat Astralians with deep respect.

22
00:01:26.056 --> 00:01:30.199
"Engage meld medallion to activate human-shaped camouflage for protection."

23
00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:32.620
"Phew!" Ally said.

24
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.062
"I can camouflage myself to look like a human.

25
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:38.804
Okay, Alpha, let's land on Earth."

26
00:01:42.426 --> 00:01:45.568
Ally watched as the pod approached the pretty blue-and-green planet.

27
00:01:45.588 --> 00:01:49.810
"Earth matches my outfit," she thought.

28
00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.251
"It can't be too bad."

29
00:01:58.348 --> 00:02:03.330
The pod flew low over a deserted sandy area before touching down behind some trees in a park.

30
00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:12.935
Ally slipped on her meld medallion, a necklace that contained special technology.

31
00:02:14.796 --> 00:02:16.957
It allowed her to blend in with other life-forms.

32
00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:23.560
She expected to feel different instantly, but instead she felt just like herself—until she looked in the mirror.

33
00:02:26.028 --> 00:02:31.350
"Wow!" Her tentacles had been transformed into red, curly hair, and her nose was now sharp and pointy.

34
00:02:32.811 --> 00:02:35.092
But the most surprising change was to her feet.

35
00:02:36.852 --> 00:02:39.393
"Ugh My feet look so small now."

36
00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:43.815
"Small feet are the least of your problems," the computer said.

37
00:02:44.355 --> 00:02:46.356
Ally ignored the comment and went outside.

38
00:02:51.598 --> 00:02:55.320
She used her meld medallion to shrink the pod and camouflage it among the trees.

39
00:02:56.672 --> 00:02:58.553
"Don't go anywhere, Alpha.

40
00:02:58.874 --> 00:03:01.075
I might need to escape quickly from this place!"

41
00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:11.483
As she stepped out from behind the trees, Ally saw some posters about local attractions along the path.

42
00:03:12.143 --> 00:03:15.786
Two humans—a mother and daughter—were looking at one of the posters.

43
00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:19.128
Ally tried to read their minds but couldn't hear anything.

44
00:03:19.848 --> 00:03:21.369
"Hmm," she thought.

45
00:03:21.389 --> 00:03:24.632
"Maybe my mind-reading ability doesn't work here."

46
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.543
She lifted her arms in a traditional Astralian greeting.

47
00:03:28.563 --> 00:03:32.206
"Hello!" The little girl spun around.

48
00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.371
alien, Mommy!

49
00:03:37.391 --> 00:03:38.992
A real one!"

50
00:03:39.653 --> 00:03:40.413
Ally froze.

51
00:03:45.498 --> 00:03:46.579
But the mother smiled.

52
00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:49.502
"That's just a friendly teenager, honey.

53
00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:51.644
Wave and say hello!"

54
00:03:57.308 --> 00:04:00.790
After the humans walked away, Ally went over to look at the posters.

55
00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:06.554
One showed a picture of a large glass building—with a GrayZonian spaceship floating above it.

56
00:04:08.055 --> 00:04:11.457
Intrigued, Ally held up her meld medallion to translate the poster.

57
00:04:12.097 --> 00:04:16.120
It read, "Visit the World-Famous Sandville UFO Museum!"

58
00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:22.504
"That sounds like the perfect place to find parts and fuel," Ally thought.

59
00:04:23.964 --> 00:04:27.647
After walking around for thirty minutes, Ally still hadn't found the museum.

60
00:04:28.107 --> 00:04:33.571
She'd been on hot planets before, but this one seemed particularly warm with a blazing sun and no

61
00:04:33.631 --> 00:04:36.854
clouds. She felt hot and hungry.

62
00:04:42.037 --> 00:04:44.159
Just then she caught a delicious scent.

63
00:04:44.179 --> 00:04:50.904
"Food!" She jumped up and followed the scent to a busy street with a crowded restaurant.

64
00:04:56.508 --> 00:04:58.269
A sign read, "Pepe's Diner.

65
00:04:58.509 --> 00:04:59.609
Grand Opening Today!"

66
00:05:03.411 --> 00:05:05.472
Ally took a deep breath and went inside.

67
00:05:10.514 --> 00:05:13.055
To her relief, nobody looked at her in surprise.

68
00:05:13.075 --> 00:05:16.177
"Good!" she thought.

69
00:05:16.197 --> 00:05:19.098
"My meld medallion is working."

70
00:05:21.879 --> 00:05:23.280
A waitress handed her a menu.

71
00:05:24.552 --> 00:05:26.254
"Only one seat is left at the counter."

72
00:05:28.736 --> 00:05:30.397
Ally sat down and opened the menu.

73
00:05:32.178 --> 00:05:36.742
She wanted to use her meld medallion to translate it, but the waitress was watching her closely.

74
00:05:40.805 --> 00:05:41.926
just have one of everything!"

75
00:05:42.266 --> 00:05:43.127
Ally blurted out.

76
00:05:43.147 --> 00:05:45.289
"You got enough money?

77
00:05:45.649 --> 00:05:47.050
That'll cost hundreds of dollars."

78
00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:51.234
"Dollars?" Ally shook her head.

79
00:05:51.254 --> 00:05:53.876
"I don't have any of those."

80
00:05:57.301 --> 00:05:58.783
The waitress took the menu back.

81
00:05:59.723 --> 00:06:01.545
"Sorry, no handouts."

82
00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:04.006
Ally was confused.

83
00:06:04.026 --> 00:06:06.989
"I didn't ask you for a hand.

84
00:06:07.469 --> 00:06:09.010
I asked for food."

85
00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:13.773
"If you want anything in this world, honey, you've got to work for it."

86
00:06:13.793 --> 00:06:17.636
"Oh!" Ally finally understood.

87
00:06:18.097 --> 00:06:22.480
Unlike on other planets where food was free, Earthlings charged money for nourishment.

88
00:06:24.004 --> 00:06:26.026
"I can pay for my meal with good deeds.

89
00:06:26.987 --> 00:06:28.968
Do you have a war that you need stopped?

90
00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:31.510
Natural resources that need protection?"

91
00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:36.294
"Ha-ha," the waitress said, but she wasn't laughing.

92
00:06:37.055 --> 00:06:39.336
"Like I said, you need to find a job."

93
00:06:39.357 --> 00:06:44.381
"How?" "Look for 'Help Wanted' signs."

94
00:06:46.042 --> 00:06:46.762
Ally grinned.

95
00:06:47.723 --> 00:06:48.704
"No problem!

96
00:06:49.044 --> 00:06:53.228
Responding to cries for help is what we Astralians do best!"

97
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:55.626
She leaped up and darted out the door.
